# Reactive Surface Phase 5 Water/Puddle Report - 2026-07-05

Verdict: PASS (corrected on 2026-07-07)

## 2026-07-07 Correction: False Wave Propagation Pass

The original Phase 5 water report is no longer valid as proof of true water-wave propagation.
Follow-up inspection found that `NS_RS_Water` did not contain the 2-step wave equation at the time of this report; it was running the curl/advection path, and `WaveSpeed` / `Damping` were orphan parameters. The old temporal/max-decay evidence proved bounded nonzero output only, not an expanding wave ring.

Corrected production proof is tracked in:

- `codex/docs/projects/cubeless-stylized/systems/evidence/reactive-surface-water-v3-height-solver-results-2026-07-07.json`
- `codex/docs/projects/cubeless-stylized/systems/evidence/reactive-surface-water-v3-production-apply-results-2026-07-07.json`

| Corrected check | Status | Numeric evidence |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Production compile | PASS | `NS_RS_Water`, errors=0, warnings=0 |
| Height expanding ring | PASS | frame radii px `[1.5, 5.42, 9.0, 13.44, 18.38]` |
| Production normal expanding ring | PASS | frame radii px `[5.73, 5.84, 9.84, 13.77, 21.05]` |
| Center stability | PASS | normal center offset stayed `<=0.69px` |
| Dependency audit | PASS | forbidden MCP refs `0` |

For future water solver review, Phase 5 should be treated as a false pass for wave propagation. The accepted criterion is a 2-step history solver plus expanding-ring evidence, not monotonic decay alone.

